10. PROTECTION OF VICTIMS, DUE PROCESS, AND PROHIBITION OF LEGAL ABUSE

10.1 Purpose and Public Interest

WFX is released publicly to support defenses against software supply-chain exploitation, unauthorized repository or workflow activity, and other security failures. Its availability must not be used to shield negligent conduct, suppress legitimate claims, or deprive affected persons of access to justice.

10.2 Express Condition of Software Licensing

This Section is an express and material condition of the copyright permissions granted under Section 0. Any recipient exercising those permissions accepts these obligations independently of participation in DPL 1.1.

10.3 Prohibited Legal Abuse

Licensees agree not to:

a. Use WFX or its licensing provisions to conceal, excuse, facilitate, or perpetuate exploitation arising from corporate negligence or security misconduct.
b. Misrepresent rights, obligations, or protections established by this License.
c. Use patent claims, contractual restrictions, litigation, or regulatory proceedings to obstruct lawful defensive mitigation or suppress legitimate claims concerning Covered Technology.
d. Invoke this License to deny affected customers access to lawful remedies.
e. Use this License or its protections to obtain immunity from accountability for conduct violating applicable law.

10.4 Automatic and Irrevocable Waiver Upon Violation

As an express condition of the permissions granted here, each licensee prospectively agrees that violating Section 10.3 triggers, to the maximum extent enforceable under applicable law, an automatic waiver of its right to invoke or enforce against affected customers, in connection with claims arising from or materially related to the violation:

a. Mandatory or compelled arbitration agreements.
b. Contractual jury-trial waivers.
c. Contractual prohibitions on collective or class proceedings.
d. Contractual restrictions on access to courts or judicial remedies.
e. Contractual limitations unlawfully restricting due process, procedural fairness, discovery, or available remedies.
f. Substantially equivalent provisions preventing affected customers from pursuing otherwise lawful claims.

This waiver is intended to apply to agreements entered into before or after acceptance, to the maximum extent enforceable under applicable law. It is a direct contractual undertaking by the licensee and does not depend on formally amending an underlying customer agreement.

10.5 Intended Third-Party Beneficiaries

Customers materially affected by a violation of Section 10.3 are intended third-party beneficiaries of Sections 10.3 and 10.4 and may, to the extent permitted by applicable law, invoke the waiver and seek declaratory, injunctive, or other available relief. No additional agreement with the Licensor is required to establish this stated intention.

10.6 Determination of Violation

A violation may be established by a court or competent tribunal. The waiver is intended to arise upon the prohibited conduct itself rather than only upon judgment; this provision does not dispense with any adjudication required by applicable law.

10.7 Preservation of Fundamental Rights

Nothing here diminishes any person's constitutional, statutory, civil, contractual, or procedural rights. Greater protections under applicable law remain available.

10.8 Survival and Severability

Obligations arising from a triggering violation survive termination to the extent permitted by law. Unenforceability of one provision or remedy does not extinguish otherwise enforceable provisions or remedies.

10.9 Relationship to Other License Provisions

This Section is part of WFX's software copyright license and does not modify DPL 1.1. Applicable provisions should be interpreted consistently with the stated protective purposes and governing law.

