11.4 Jurisdiction-Specific Application

Where a provision is unenforceable, the remainder continues to the fullest extent permitted by law, and any permissible adaptation should preserve its protective purpose.

11.5 Application of Future Revisions

Revisions apply prospectively to recipients accepting the revised License and to existing relationships only where permitted by applicable law and their governing terms. No revision automatically creates retroactive obligations or binds nonconsenting parties where law forbids it. Independently available legal rights remain preserved.

11.6 Declaration of Forced Hand

This defensive publication is made in recognition that security threats can require a public response before every conventional legal formality is complete. The Licensor intends that publication urgency not itself deny affected persons otherwise available protection or remedy.

